It seems as if pretty much everyone is in agreement that a mode of
ranged attack being critical in survival depth for new players.
Wizards and Rangers both start with this excellent advantage at their
disposal.

I too found early on that my =91best=92 characters were with these two
classes.  I think Rangers ultimately surpass Wizards in survival depth
of new players for several previously stated reasons; available armor,
health, and melee skills.  Sure the wizard=92s magic is =91infinite=92 and
powerful, but you must show experience and patience by not wasting
your available magic blasting everything you see.  Beginners simply do
not have this built up experience, knowing when and when not to use up
their arsenal, what creatures are truly dangerous and when to
preemptively flee a level or encounter.

With the Ranger you don=92t have to know or think about any of the
traditional nethack tricks; simply arrow spam everything, put on
